2026-09-27T03:28:14.9512097Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9512470Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9512786Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9513615Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9514625Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9514728Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9514935Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9515238Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9515548Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9515647Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9515905Z ================
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9516057Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9516225Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9516629Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9516887Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9517031Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9517545Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9517742Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9517916Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9518358Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9518755Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9519503Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9520124Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9520258Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9520765Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9521422Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9521757Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9522127Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9522604Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9522708Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9523044Z ========
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9523181Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9524645Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9526267Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9526533Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9527084Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9527938Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9528634Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9529294Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9593865Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9594231Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9594873Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9595299Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9595535Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9596690Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9597976Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9598457Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9599124Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:28:14.9599281Z 
